{"id":"resp_bd79e8182add53dc","created_at":1795617866,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_982422126997ab13","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce SHACL graph representing requirement TRF-018: engine output shall not be less than formula and not less than 1,000 kW for IA, IB, IC and not less than 2,800 kW for IA Super.\n\nWe have ontology terms: calculatedRequiredPower (quantity property) with domain benchmarkEntity and range QuantityValue. Also iceClass property linking benchmarkEntity to iceClassValue individuals (IA, IA Super, IB, IC, etc.)\n\nTerm owners: calculatedRequiredPower owner ship (owner_class ship). IceClass also owned by ship. maximumContinuousRatingPower also owned by ship.\n\nWe need to create SHACL shapes targeting ship class: targetClass https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship\n\nWithin shape, we need constraints:\n\n- For ships with iceClass IA Super, calculatedRequiredPower must be >= 2800 kW.\n\n- For ships with iceClass IA, IB, IC, calculatedRequiredPower must be >= 1000 kW.\n\nQuantity encoding: use qudt:numericValue and qudt:unit.\n\nWe need to represent constraints using sh:property with sh:path referencing calculatedRequiredPower, and sh:minCount? Actually need numeric constraint: sh:datatype xsd:decimal maybe, and sh:minInclusive? For quantity we need to enforce numeric value when unit is kW.\n\nWe need to capture unit requirement: also ensure unit is kW? Could use sh:qualifiedValueShape with property path of calculatedRequiredPower then within that shape enforce both numeric and unit.\n\nSimplify: Use sh:property with sh:path calculatedRequiredPower ; sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI? Actually calculatedRequiredPower points to QuantityValue node which is a blank node with qudt:numericValue and qudt:unit. So we need a sh:property with sh:path calculatedRequiredPower and sh:node (or sh:nodeShape) that checks numeric value.\n\nDefine shape for ship with iceClass IA Super etc using sh:or to select appropriate class.\n\nApproach: Create two shapes with sh:targetClass ship but with sh:condition based on iceClass value. In SHACL we can use sh:property with sh:qualifiedValueShape that includes sh:class iceClassIaSuper? Actually iceClass property points to iceClassValue individual. So we need to filter ships where iceClass = iceClassIaSuper. Use sh:property with sh:path iceClass and sh:hasValue <...> inside shape? Could use sh:property with sh:path iceClass; sh:hasValue <...>. But that would enforce that ship must have that value; we want condition for constraint only. We can use sh:if (sh:condition) maybe using sh:sparql? Simpler: Use SHACL SPARQL constraint to enforce rule: For each ship, if iceClass is IA Super then the calculatedRequiredPower's numericValue >= 2800; else if iceClass is IA, IB, IC then >=1000.\n\nWe'll implement a sh:property for calculatedRequiredPower with sh:datatype xsd:decimal, but numeric check using sh:minInclusive with separate shapes? Not straightforward.\n\nBetter: Use sh:sparql constraint on ship shape:\n\nsh:sparql [\n  a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;\n  sh:message \"Engine output must be at least 2800 kW for IA Super ships.\" ;\n  sh:select \"\"\"\n    SELECT $this ( ?value ) WHERE {\n      $this <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClassIaSuper> .\n      $this <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#calculatedRequiredPower> ?cp .\n      ?cp <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue> ?val .\n      ?cp <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit> <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloW> .\n      FILTER ( ?val < 2800 )\n    }\n  \"\"\" ;\n] .\n\nAnother for IA, IB, IC with threshold 1000.\n\nThus need two sh:SPARQLConstraint.\n\nDefine shape with targetClass ship.\n\nAdd prefixes.\n\nMake sure IRIs correct.\n\nAlso need to include requirement evidence maybe using rdfs:comment.\n\nWe must not invent missing owners etc. Owner is ship already.\n\nProvide <BEGIN_SHACL> line then Turtle.\n\nLet's craft.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_9c4a96fa92c972fd","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n\n# Shape applying to all ships (the admitted synthetic population)\nnltl:ShipEngineOutputShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    \n    # Constraint for IA Super ships – minimum 2 800 kW\n    sh:sparql [\n        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;\n        rdfs:comment \"The engine output shall not be less than 2 800 kW for ice class IA Super (TRF‑018).\" ;\n        sh:message \"Engine output for IA Super ships must be ≥ 2 800 kW.\" ;\n        sh:select \"\"\"\n            SELECT $this ?val WHERE {\n                $this nltl:iceClass nltl:iceClassIaSuper .\n                $this nltl:calculatedRequiredPower ?cp .\n                ?cp qudt:numericValue ?val .\n                ?cp qudt:unit unit:KiloW .\n                FILTER ( ?val < 2800 )\n            }\n        \"\"\" ;\n    ] ;\n    \n    # Constraint for IA, IB, IC ships – minimum 1 000 kW\n    sh:sparql [\n        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;\n        rdfs:comment \"The engine output shall not be less than 1 000 kW for ice classes IA, IB and IC (TRF‑018).\" ;\n        sh:message \"Engine output for IA, IB, or IC ships must be ≥ 1 000 kW.\" ;\n        sh:select \"\"\"\n            SELECT $this ?val WHERE {\n                $this nltl:iceClass ?ic .\n                FILTER ( ?ic IN (nltl:iceClassIa, nltl:iceClassIb, nltl:iceClassIc) )\n                $this nltl:calculatedRequiredPower ?cp .\n                ?cp qudt:numericValue ?val .\n                ?cp qudt:unit unit:KiloW .\n                FILTER ( ?val < 1000 )\n            }\n        \"\"\" ;\n    ] .\n\n# Declaration of the quantity value class (required for the value nodes)\nunit:KiloW a rdf:Property .   # placeholder to ensure the IRI is known in the graph\n\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":36975,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":592,"cache_write_tokens":36368,"input_tokens_per_turn":[36975],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[592]},"output_tokens":1538,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":912,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1538],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":38513},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}